    intro: "Monica Ali's Brick Lane (2003) is a standalone debut novel following Nazneen, an eighteen-year-old Bangladeshi woman who arrives in London for an arranged marriage with the older, kind, garrulous Chanu, and who over the next two decades makes herself at home in the Tower Hamlets housing estate and falls into an affair with a younger man. Shortlisted for the Booker Prize and one of the defining novels of British South Asian immigrant experience.",
