    intro: "Maggie Nelson's The Argonauts (2015) is a hybrid memoir combining autobiography, queer theory, and philosophy, following her relationship with the fluidly gendered artist Harry Dodge, her pregnancy and the birth of their son, and Harry's testosterone treatments and top surgery, all interleaved with thinkers from Roland Barthes to D.W. Winnicott. Winner of the National Book Critics Circle Award for Criticism.",
