    slug: 'old-times-pinter',
    intro: "Old Times (1971) by Harold Pinter is a play about memory, possession, and the past — or rather, about the impossibility of recovering the past and the violence of competing claims about what it was. Anna arrives to visit her old friend Kate and Kate's husband Deeley, and over the course of the evening the relationship between the three of them becomes increasingly strange: who knew Kate first; what happened between Anna and Kate in the London flat they shared twenty years ago; what Deeley's relationship to both women actually is. Pinter called the play his most autobiographical work, and it is organized around the same question that all his plays organized: who tells the true story of the past? The play's answer is that memory is not a record of what happened but a weapon used to claim territory — and that the territory being claimed is always a person.",
