    slug: 'une-vie-maupassant',
    intro: "A Life (Une Vie, 1883) by Guy de Maupassant is the author's first novel and his most sustained portrait of a woman whose life is systematically destroyed by the men around her — the story of Jeanne de Lamare, a young aristocratic woman in Normandy who marries in hope and spends the next forty years watching her illusions collapse through her husband's infidelities and cruelties, her son's extravagance and selfishness, and the indifference of the world to her suffering. Maupassant described it as 'the story of a woman's whole life, her hopes, fears, love and disillusionment' — a deliberately anti-romantic account of what Flaubert's Madame Bovary might have looked like told from outside rather than inside the romantic consciousness.",
