    slug: 'the-american-james',
    intro: "The American (1877) by Henry James is the author's first major international novel and the work in which he first articulated the theme that would define his career — the encounter between American optimism and European complexity. Christopher Newman, a wealthy, good-natured, self-made American businessman, arrives in Paris determined to 'have the best of everything' and decides that what he wants is a beautiful, accomplished wife from the European aristocracy. He falls in love with Claire de Cintré, a French widow from the Bellegarde family, and her family accepts his courtship — until, for reasons Newman cannot fully understand, the Bellegarde family withdraws their approval and Claire enters a Carmelite convent. The novel is organized around Newman's gradual comprehension that he has encountered something beyond his understanding: an aristocratic social logic that no amount of money can overcome.",
