    intro: "C.S. Lewis's The Chronicles of Narnia (1950–1956) is a seven-volume fantasy series set in the magical land of Narnia, created by the great Lion Aslan and reached through various means — a wardrobe, a painting, a pool, a door. Lewis and Tolkien were close friends at Oxford and members of the same literary group (the Inklings), though they disagreed about the proper approach to fantasy: Tolkien felt Narnia's mixing of mythologies (Greek, Roman, Norse, and Christian) was aesthetically incoherent; Lewis didn't care. The best reading order is disputed: Lewis himself suggested chronological order starting with The Magician's Nephew (the creation of Narnia), but most readers and publishers recommend publication order starting with The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe, which Lewis wrote first and which makes the best entry point.",
