    intro: "Vikram Seth's A Suitable Boy (1993) is one of the longest novels written in the English language and one of the most beloved — a vast, warm, meticulously observed portrait of post-independence India in 1951, following four interconnected families across the fictional city of Brahmpur as Mrs. Rupa Mehra searches for a suitable husband for her youngest daughter, Lata. The novel moves through Hindu-Muslim relations, land reform, the first national elections, romantic love, political intrigue, and the textures of everyday Indian life with a comprehensiveness and affection that recall Tolstoy. Seth wrote it over ten years, producing a manuscript of more than 1,300 pages; it is one of the few novels of that length that readers consistently describe as impossible to put down. Its companion novel, A Suitable Girl (forthcoming), continues the story into the present.",
