    slug: 'the-leopard',
    intro: "Giuseppe Tomasi di Lampedusa's The Leopard (1958) is the great novel of Sicily and one of the supreme achievements of Italian fiction — the story of Don Fabrizio Corbera, Prince of Salina, as he watches the unification of Italy destroy the world he was born into and remake it in ways that leave no place for him. The novel covers the years 1860 to 1910, from Garibaldi's landing in Sicily through the protagonist's death and its aftermath, but it is primarily a meditation on change and how the aristocratic mind understands it — 'Everything must change so that everything can stay the same' is the novel's most famous line. Lampedusa wrote the novel in the 1950s and died in 1957 before its publication; it was rejected by two publishers before being accepted by Feltrinelli, which published it posthumously to immediate acclaim.",
