    slug: 'middle-passage',
    intro: "Charles Johnson's Middle Passage (1990) won the National Book Award and is one of the most formally ambitious and intellectually demanding American novels of the late twentieth century — a sea-adventure novel set in 1830 aboard the slave ship Republic, narrated by the freed slave Rutherford Calhoun. The novel borrows its structure from Melville's Moby-Dick (sea voyage, obsessive captain, strange cargo) and uses it to explore the history of the trans-Atlantic slave trade, African philosophy, and the question of what freedom means when it is achieved within systems that do not recognize Black humanity.",
