    intro: "Charles Dickens's Hard Times (1854) is his most explicitly political novel — a direct attack on Utilitarianism, the philosophy that reduced human beings to units of economic calculation, and on the industrial capitalism that reduced workers to 'Hands.' Set in the fictional northern industrial town of Coketown, it is Dickens's shortest novel and his most didactic, but also the one that most clearly states the moral argument that underlies all his fiction: that imagination, sympathy, and human connection are necessary to life, and that any system that suppresses them is morally criminal.",
