    intro: "Thomas Hardy's Tess of the d'Urbervilles: A Pure Woman Faithfully Presented (1891) is one of the most powerful and disturbing novels in the English tradition — the story of Tess Durbeyfield, a young country woman who is raped by the aristocrat Alec d'Urberville, loses the resulting child, falls in love with the idealistic Angel Clare, and is destroyed by a society that refuses to allow her the title 'pure' after what was done to her. The subtitle is Hardy's defiant argument.",
