    slug: 'the-sound-and-the-fury',
    intro: "William Faulkner's The Sound and the Fury (1929) is one of the most formally daring and psychologically intense novels in American literature — the story of the decline of the Compson family in Mississippi, told four times from four different perspectives, including the opening section narrated by Benjy, who is cognitively disabled and experiences time non-linearly. The novel requires active participation from the reader and rewards it with one of the most complete portraits of grief and loss in fiction.",
