    slug: 'never-split-the-difference',
    intro: "Chris Voss's Never Split the Difference: Negotiating as if Your Life Depended on It (2016) draws on Voss's fifteen years as the FBI's lead international kidnapping negotiator to present a framework for negotiation built on emotional intelligence rather than rational game theory — arguing that the key tools are tactical empathy, active listening, and a set of specific techniques (mirroring, labeling, the 'accusation audit,' calibrated questions) that create trust and influence without compromise.",
