    intro: "Seneca's Letters from a Stoic (Epistulae Morales ad Lucilium, c. 63–65 CE) is the most accessible and humanely written of all the Stoic texts — 124 letters from the Roman philosopher and statesman to his friend Lucilius, covering friendship, time, death, poverty, illness, pleasure, anger, and what it means to live a good life. Written in the final years of Seneca's life during a self-imposed retirement from Nero's court, they are at once personal, philosophical, and remarkably contemporary.",
