    slug: 'mexican-gothic',
    intro: "Silvia Moreno-Garcia's Mexican Gothic (2020) is a Gothic horror novel set in 1950s Mexico, following socialite Noemí Taboada as she travels to a crumbling manor called High Place in the Mexican countryside to investigate her cousin Catalina's deteriorating mental state. What she finds in the English expatriate Doyle family's house is a nightmare of colonial violence, biological horror, and a house that thinks and breathes and controls the living. A deliberate homage to the classic Gothic tradition — Rebecca, The Haunting of Hill House, We Have Always Lived in the Castle — transplanted to a Mexican context and refracted through the history of colonial exploitation.",
    startWith: 'Mexican Gothic',
