    slug: 'educated',
    intro: "Tara Westover's Educated (2018) is a memoir about growing up in a survivalist family in the mountains of rural Idaho — her parents believed the government was preparing for the End of Days and refused to send their children to school or allow doctors to treat their injuries — and her journey from that world through self-education to a PhD from Cambridge University. One of the bestselling memoirs of its decade, Educated is about intellectual awakening, family loyalty, and the cost of choosing your own version of reality over the one your family insists on.",
